From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MRQC-st <18975964597@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 05:48:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: assistant phases for Codex clients alone; muse
 killed its run on a later commentary
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

their phase, holding a message's output_item.done until what follows says
whether it was commentary or the answer. The text deltas go out live, so a
client that reads the stream strictly already has the item as the final
answer when the done arrives saying commentary — and Muse Code takes that
for a fatal protocol regression ("stream protocol error: message item …
changed phase from final_answer to commentary"), kills its whole run, and
retries nothing. Every muse turn that streamed text before a tool call
died this way; of 124 turns that reached a tool call without text first,
none did (magpie usage, 2026-10-30, muse 1.4.14 on deepseek via CodeArts
and lobster, /v1/responses → /v1/chat/completions).

The phase exists for Codex's folding alone (#2437), so it is written for
Codex's requests alone: codexPhase (fromCodex or agentOf "codex") gates
phaseTidy in passthrough, and Request.phaseClient — set in
streamTranslated and relay — carries the same gate to responsesEncoder
(no phase written, and a message's done no longer held) and to
renderResponses. Codex's replies are byte for byte what they were;
every other client gets the reply as it streamed, with no wait.

Real muse exec against the encoder's bytes: the text-then-tool stream
failed before, completes after. New: TestOtherClientGetsNoPhase,
TestMuseClientStreamHasNoPhase. TestRelayedStreamSaysPhase's codexPostTo
now names Codex's User-Agent and Originator, as the real client's turn
does. Doc: gateway-routing.md's phase paragraph.

Run: go test -tags nogui -timeout 45m ./internal/gateway/ (ok, 461.6s),
go vet -tags nogui ./internal/gateway/, gofmt -l, go build -tags nogui
./...

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
